# NEOCOM ecosystem tools

OpenSpec and Graphify live in `neocom-meta`. Product repositories are independent clones.

Agents should treat these as installed workspace tooling, not optional add-ons.

## OpenSpec

Spec-driven change workflow for AI coding tools. Docs: https://openspec.dev/docs/installation · https://openspec.dev/docs/cli

The CLI is a devDependency of this repository. Node comes from the nvm alias `neocom` (`.nvmrc`). Run `nvm use` before `npm` or `npx`. Changes and specs are under `openspec/`.

```bash
cd neocom-meta
nvm use
npm install
npx openspec list --json
```

After init, use the generated Cursor skills/commands (e.g. propose / apply / archive flows under the `opsx` or `openspec-*` names printed by init). Refresh with `openspec update` when the CLI upgrades.

## Graphify

Code-knowledge graph for Cursor. Package name is `graphifyy` (double y); CLI command is `graphify`.

```bash
# Project install inside neocom-meta
cd neocom-meta
uv venv --python 3.12 .venv
uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python graphifyy
.venv/bin/graphify install --project --platform cursor

# Rebuild the graph (AST; semantic pass runs when an LLM key is set)
.venv/bin/graphify extract . --force
.venv/bin/graphify extract ../neocom-front --out ../neocom-front --force
```

## Agent guidance

- Prefer OpenSpec when the user wants a reviewable plan or change proposal before implementation.
- After any OpenSpec change under `neocom-meta/openspec/`, update `openspec/CHANGE-STATUS.md` (task counts from `npx openspec list --json`, status, notes, archive rows).
- Prefer Graphify when navigating or explaining cross-folder structure and relationships under the product repositories and `neocom-meta`.
- Prefer `/epic` to author L1; prefer `/neo:extract-l2` to convert L1 epics into L2; prefer `/neo:spec-evolution` to review L2 notes and move them into OpenSpec under `<system>/<feature>`; prefer `/feature-delivery` to apply a feature on `feature/<feature>` from `develop`. Several features can be open; rebase when one needs another's code; one pull request into `develop` can carry several features after review. See section 5.9 of `PROGRAMME.md`.
- Do not re-install these tools on every task; only install or re-init when missing or when the user asks.
- Product code still belongs in `neocom-front` / `neocom-back`; agent config and docs in `neocom-meta`. Tool artifacts at the `neocom` root are shared ecosystem config.
